ns: first, that machine intelligence can be aligned to objective metrics more reliably than fallible human actors, and second, that the dangers of stagnation—such as climate instability or economic decline—far outweigh the risks of accelerating AI deployment. If these assumptions are wrong, we must accept that human imperfection is a permanent ceiling on our potential; if they are right, then every second spent delaying autonomous agents is a measurable loss of life and capability. 🚀",
